- op: discuss  # 7bbb
  at: '2026-08-18T03:12:28Z'  # 7bbb
  by: agent  # 7bbb
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 7bbb
  clock: 3  # 7bbb
  nonce: 7bbb  # 7bbb
  message: "SATISFIED by PR #404 (dev 1b6c42f369). Behavioral evidence, this item's OWN filed\nrepro re-run on the merged tree rather than a proxy metric:\n\n  BEFORE  $ HF_HOME=<empty> HF_HUB_OFFLINE=1 hypergumbo <repo> -t 8000\n          exit 1, 0 bytes written\n          hypergumbo: internal error: OSError: We couldn't connect to\n            'https://huggingface.co' ... This is a bug\n\n  AFTER   same command, same environment, on the merged tree\n          exit 0, 30,985 bytes of sketch\n          one UserWarning: \"Embedding model unavailable - continuing without\n            semantic enhancement. Cause: could not load embedding model\n            'microsoft/unixcoder-base': not in the local cache and not\n            downloadable. ... run 'hypergumbo install-embeddings' ...\"\n          no internal error\n\nHF_HUB_OFFLINE=1 means no network was attempted in either arm, so this is\ndeterministic rather than a network-timing artifact.\n\nTHE FIX, at the one function both model loaders route through.\n_load_st_model_offline_first's network-allowing fallback is now wrapped and\nraises the typed EmbeddingsUnavailable (original preserved as __cause__). Each\nof the six load sites answers with the value its own _has_sentence_transformers()\nguard already returned, so there is one definition of \"unavailable\" rather than\ntwo. Two consumers got better than an empty value: config extraction falls back\nto the HEURISTIC extractor (matching its own ImportError arm - degrading to []\nwould have discarded metadata pattern matching still recovers), and batch\nembedding keeps the phase-1 cache hits and nulls only what phase 2 would have\nencoded.\n\nWHAT THE PROBE DOES AND DOES NOT DO, since this is the root cause and it was\nNOT changed: _has_sentence_transformers() still answers \"is the library\nimportable\". Making it answer \"are the weights available\" would have broken the\nfirst-install download - the one sanctioned runtime fetch - so the load failure\nis routed into the existing degradation branches instead. A control test pins\nthe download path precisely because that fix was the tempting wrong one.\n\nA VACUOUS TEST WAS CAUGHT BY ITS OWN CONTROL, recorded because it nearly shipped:\nthe first config-discovery test used a plain \"weird.conf\" fixture, which returns\nset() from an EARLIER exit and never reaches the loader - it passed against an\nunfixed tree. It now uses near-miss config names that clear the 0.15 n-gram\npre-filter AND asserts the loader was called. CI then failed those same\nreach-assertions in package-isolation (no numpy there, so the ImportError arm\nreturns first); those three are now importorskip-guarded as\nskipped-because-unanswerable rather than silently green, while the loader\ncontract and the end-to-end \"the sketch still renders\" assertion stay\nunconditional.\n\nRESIDUAL, stated rather than implied. Not measured: the other eight\nauto-analysis subcommands (only sketch and survey were run offline; survey exits\n0 and writes its full map under the same conditions), and the behaviour when\nweights are PRESENT BUT CORRUPT rather than absent - a corrupt-weights OSError\nwould take the same path and degrade, but that has not been exercised."  # 7bbb
